<description>
Copy every solid foreground rectangle repeatedly along both downward diagonal directions, clipping copies at the grid edge.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- There is one foreground color.
- Each 4-connected foreground object is a filled axis-aligned rectangle.

Rule
- Keep the original rectangles.
- For a rectangle of height h and width w, stamp the same rectangle at offsets (h, -w), (2h, -2w), ... and (h, w), (2h, 2w), ...
- Drop only the out-of-bounds part of any stamped rectangle and stop once a trajectory is fully outside the grid.

Key insight
- Each rectangle is both the sprite and the stride: its height controls the downward step and its width controls the sideways step.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "each filled foreground rectangle s",
  "path": "two downward diagonal paths from s, stepping by s.height rows and by +/-s.width columns until the stamped rectangle is fully outside the grid",
  "trajectory": "copy s at every step, dropping any cells that fall outside the grid",
  "transform": "keep the original rectangles and union all copied foreground pixels on the background"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 25-29 rows x 22-29 cols
  background: 0 (black)
  foreground: single color (always 3/green in eval) [observed]
  rectangles:
    count: 1-3 solid filled axis-aligned rectangles
    height: 2-4
    width: 2-5
    area: 6-10
    position: placed in upper portion so room_below/height >= 3 (ensures >=2 stamps downward per direction)
    separation: non-overlapping, well-separated (row_sep >= 2, col_sep >= 4)
  trajectory:
    directions: two downward diagonals from each rect, stepping (h, -w) and (h, +w)
    stamps_per_direction: 2-12 (at least 2 in every direction)
    clipping: some stamps partially exit grid laterally (2-4 clipped stamps per example)
    total_stamps: 5-25 per example
  output: same grid with all stamped copies unioned onto background

generation_strategy:
